# One gradient-descent step for a one-parameter linear model.
features is [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
targets is [2.0, 4.0, 6.0]
mut slope as Float is 0.0
learning_rate is 0.1

predictions is vector_scale(features, slope)
errors is vector_subtract(predictions, targets)
mse is dot(errors, errors) / length(features)
gradient is 2.0 * dot(features, errors) / length(features)
slope -> slope - learning_rate * gradient

Sayln mse
Sayln slope
